{title: Lord Who Throughout These Forty Days}
{key: C}
{time: 6/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Lord [C]who through[F]out these [Am]forty [F]days
For [C]us didst [Dm]fast and [G]pray[**]
Teach [Am]us with [Em]Thee to [F]mourn our [G]sins
And [Am]close by [F]Thee to [C]stay[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
As [C]Thou with [F]Satan [Am]didst con[F]tend
And [C]didst the [Dm]victory [G]win[**]
O [Am]give us [Em]strength in [F]Thee to [G]fight
In [Am]Thee to [F]conquer [C]sin[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
As [C]Thou didst [F]hunger [Am]bear and [F]thirst
So [C]teach us [Dm]gracious [G]Lord[**]
To [Am]die to [Em]self and [F]chiefly [G]live
By [Am]Thy most [F]holy [C]word[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
And [C]through these [F]days of [Am]peni[F]tence
And [C]through Thy [Dm]passion[G]tide[**]
Yea [Am]ever[Em]more in [F]life and [G]death
Je[Am]sus with [F]us a[C]bide[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 5}
A[C]bide with [F]us that [Am]so this [F]life
Of [C]suffering [Dm]over [G]past[**]
An [Am]Easter [Em]of un[F]ending [G]joy
We [Am]may at[F]tain at [C]last[**]
{end_of_verse}
